WEBVTT

00:42.542 --> 00:45.962
SOLD OUT ON YOU

00:47.714 --> 00:51.009
When I offered to bring you
Gojeuneok Bio's raw material,

00:51.092 --> 00:52.844
didn't you already know

00:52.927 --> 00:54.888
that it was just a temporary solution?

00:54.971 --> 00:56.055
So,

00:56.931 --> 00:58.683
what are you suggesting?

01:00.143 --> 01:02.771
Gojeuneok Bio just started developing
a new product.

01:03.938 --> 01:06.316
They're making cosmetics themselves?

01:06.399 --> 01:07.275
Yes.

01:12.864 --> 01:15.617
This isn't something to smile about.

01:18.953 --> 01:21.915
There was an incident five years ago

01:21.998 --> 01:23.917
that shook the whole country.

01:24.417 --> 01:26.044
The Good Morning Cream incident.

01:27.212 --> 01:29.130
And Lee Hae-seok

01:29.214 --> 01:31.508
is the one who made that cream.

01:33.134 --> 01:35.136
Once may have been a mistake,

01:35.220 --> 01:37.680
but if it keeps happening,

01:38.556 --> 01:39.933
that's intentional.

01:41.518 --> 01:42.769
This time,

01:44.729 --> 01:47.649
I'm going to make sure he can never
set foot in this industry again.

01:53.404 --> 01:54.739
I'm here.

01:56.407 --> 01:57.867
Mechoori.

02:01.704 --> 02:02.705
You're home.

02:02.789 --> 02:04.249
What is all this?

02:05.166 --> 02:07.085
Things I have to study.

02:07.168 --> 02:09.838
Regulations have changed a lot
in the past five years,

02:09.921 --> 02:12.632
and there are loads of new methods,
so I have a lot to catch up on.

02:13.174 --> 02:16.261
Aren't you tired
after working in the lab all day?

02:17.554 --> 02:18.680
Not at all.

02:20.098 --> 02:21.766
I have some stuff to read too.

03:05.935 --> 03:07.145
Focus.

03:15.403 --> 03:18.197
Stop distracting me with your beauty.

03:26.497 --> 03:28.791
Look at the time.

03:28.875 --> 03:30.084
Aren't you going to bed?

03:31.336 --> 03:32.337
After I finish this.

03:33.171 --> 03:35.340
Someone used to hate that phrase.

03:38.927 --> 03:40.345
Fine, I'll cut you some slack.

03:40.428 --> 03:42.388
You'd better go to bed after that one.

03:42.472 --> 03:44.057
Okay. Goodnight.

03:44.140 --> 03:45.558
Goodnight.

04:25.306 --> 04:27.600
Hey, you said you'd go to bed
after that file.

04:33.064 --> 04:34.274
Did you have trouble sleeping?

04:35.108 --> 04:36.484
I couldn't sleep at all.

04:43.533 --> 04:45.493
I decided to stop taking sleeping pills.

04:46.369 --> 04:47.912
You're not taking them anymore?

04:48.579 --> 04:49.914
Why? That's sudden.

04:50.415 --> 04:54.377
I just made the decision
after watching you earlier.

04:55.044 --> 04:56.504
I want to move forward like you too.

05:00.008 --> 05:02.802
I thought the past was holding me back,

05:03.720 --> 05:05.763
but I just realized it was myself.

05:06.514 --> 05:09.350
I'm going to break free
from the cycle of insomnia

05:09.434 --> 05:10.768
and stop taking the pills.

05:13.438 --> 05:15.732
That's all good,
but just take them tonight.

05:16.607 --> 05:18.943
You should consult your doctor tomorrow.

05:19.861 --> 05:22.280
You need to taper off gradually…

05:22.363 --> 05:23.531
No.

05:23.614 --> 05:26.034
After all the sleep I lost,
I'm not taking them now.

05:30.079 --> 05:31.122
Let's go to bed now, then.

05:34.000 --> 05:36.419
I just can't sleep.

05:40.506 --> 05:42.592
You don't have
to light the candle for me tonight.

05:42.675 --> 05:44.469
Go and sleep. You must be tired.

05:47.305 --> 05:49.223
I'm going to sleep here.

06:08.409 --> 06:09.410
Are your muscles relaxed?

06:10.453 --> 06:11.454
Yes.

06:15.958 --> 06:16.959
You got it, right?

06:18.669 --> 06:22.715
Loosen your muscles, starting from
your face down to your arms and legs.

06:22.799 --> 06:27.303
Just imagine that you're a jellyfish
floating in the ocean.

06:27.845 --> 06:31.849
Why would I be a jellyfish?
What on earth is this?

06:31.933 --> 06:35.186
It's a sleep method developed
by an American sports psychologist.

06:36.437 --> 06:40.483
According to the article, this will
allow you to fall asleep in two minutes.

06:40.566 --> 06:42.401
That sounds fake.

06:42.485 --> 06:44.278
-I'm wide awake.
-Focus.

06:46.322 --> 06:48.574
You are a jellyfish.

06:50.451 --> 06:51.744
Right. I'm a jellyfish.

06:51.828 --> 06:53.037
Close your eyes…

06:53.955 --> 06:56.707
and visualize what I say.

06:57.291 --> 07:00.962
You're lying in a canoe
floating on a calm lake

07:01.045 --> 07:03.589
on a warm spring day,

07:04.215 --> 07:07.135
looking up at the clear blue sky.

07:09.679 --> 07:11.055
That's right.

07:11.139 --> 07:12.598
I'm starting to feel drowsy.

07:12.682 --> 07:13.516
That's it.

07:14.767 --> 07:15.726
Good.

07:17.687 --> 07:20.982
That guy swimming over there is jacked.

07:22.108 --> 07:23.568
Are you here alone?

07:26.654 --> 07:27.738
Stop that!

07:28.739 --> 07:31.534
What? You told me to visualize it.

07:31.617 --> 07:33.286
Stop thinking.

07:33.369 --> 07:37.915
You have to consciously
tell yourself to stop thinking.

07:37.999 --> 07:39.333
That's what the article said.

07:39.417 --> 07:41.043
Geez, I was enjoying myself.

07:41.752 --> 07:44.046
-Then let me go back to the lake.
-The lake's all dry now.

07:44.130 --> 07:45.423
Just imagine

07:47.049 --> 07:48.968
that you're lying

07:49.802 --> 07:53.347
in a black hammock in complete darkness.

07:57.477 --> 08:00.271
Alone with you, Mechoori?

08:03.441 --> 08:04.567
Stop joking around.

08:04.650 --> 08:07.445
I'm just curious.

08:08.654 --> 08:12.366
How would we lie
side by side in a hammock?

08:13.034 --> 08:14.243
I'm warning you.

08:16.621 --> 08:19.540
Don't think. Just focus.

08:36.807 --> 08:38.100
You should sleep.

08:38.809 --> 08:40.978
You said you have to head out
early tomorrow.

09:01.832 --> 09:02.875
I won't think.

10:04.645 --> 10:06.939
HIT HOMESHOPPING

10:07.023 --> 10:10.318
The coffee addict
is refusing to drink coffee?

10:11.527 --> 10:13.446
Habits are addictive too.

10:13.529 --> 10:15.072
I made up my mind to change.

10:23.039 --> 10:24.123
Is it good?

10:25.124 --> 10:25.958
But…

10:26.834 --> 10:29.378
can we move into the shade? It's too hot.

10:30.921 --> 10:35.676
We have to get at least 15 minutes
of sunlight every day.

10:38.387 --> 10:39.847
Is this a PSA or what?

10:40.389 --> 10:42.141
That's very helpful.

10:42.224 --> 10:45.436
I should get in shape
before my own program starts.

10:48.606 --> 10:49.732
You mean Dam Ye-jin's Only1?

10:50.900 --> 10:52.735
We're in the weekend
prime time slot again?

10:52.818 --> 10:56.155
You'd better take good care
of your health. Understand?

11:01.744 --> 11:02.703
Sung-mi?

11:03.287 --> 11:04.830
You understand, right?

11:07.333 --> 11:08.834
We did it!

11:08.918 --> 11:10.961
-That hurts.
-We made it!

11:13.589 --> 11:15.675
You have an item in mind, right?

11:15.758 --> 11:19.095
No, I have to start searching
for the perfect item.

11:19.178 --> 11:20.805
It's going to take ages.

11:20.888 --> 11:23.140
-Let's do this!
-Let's do this!

11:28.396 --> 11:31.482
WHITE FLOWER NOORI MUSHROOM EXTRACT

11:45.579 --> 11:47.915
So this is a new ingredient

11:47.998 --> 11:50.626
extracted from the white flower
noori mushroom with a new method?

11:51.210 --> 11:53.504
The wound's closing up much faster.

11:53.587 --> 11:55.464
Yes. See the incline here?

11:56.048 --> 11:57.842
I used this as the main ingredient,

11:57.925 --> 12:00.010
and it boosted the recovery speed
by 50 percent.

12:01.345 --> 12:03.305
I think I can create a cream

12:04.348 --> 12:05.683
that maximizes skin regeneration.

12:07.852 --> 12:08.853
Listen carefully.

12:09.437 --> 12:11.355
If you need anything,
just submit a request.

12:11.439 --> 12:13.274
Submit anything!
I'll get everything for you.

12:15.484 --> 12:18.446
You really are working hard.

12:18.529 --> 12:19.447
Hey!

12:19.530 --> 12:21.615
Remember the tofu and kimchi place
we always went to?

12:21.699 --> 12:22.992
They're still in business.

12:23.075 --> 12:25.744
Goodness, I didn't know that.

12:25.828 --> 12:27.163
Anyway, great timing.

12:27.246 --> 12:29.206
We were just about to celebrate.

12:29.290 --> 12:30.541
Why? Is there good news?

12:32.376 --> 12:35.880
Gojeuneok Bio's first cosmetic product
has just been decided.

12:35.963 --> 12:37.631
It'll be a regenerative cream.

12:39.175 --> 12:41.427
Mr. Lee here developed a new material

12:41.510 --> 12:43.721
with the white flower noori mushroom…

12:44.638 --> 12:45.473
and he slayed.

12:47.766 --> 12:50.227
What do I do? I love you so much.

12:50.311 --> 12:51.854
You want me to cut it out?

12:51.937 --> 12:54.231
Anyway, LFI.

12:55.149 --> 12:56.442
Look forward to it.

12:57.526 --> 12:58.569
Right.

12:58.652 --> 13:00.613
Anyway, congrats.

13:01.405 --> 13:03.657
But you should be cautious.

13:03.741 --> 13:06.952
Your raw material is already expensive,

13:07.036 --> 13:10.498
so with processing added,
the unit price will be pretty high.

13:10.581 --> 13:12.917
Then you won't have an advantage
in the market.

13:13.000 --> 13:15.169
Did you forget? I'm Kang Mu-won.

13:15.252 --> 13:17.129
If I was after money,
I wouldn't have started.

13:17.213 --> 13:20.633
Mu-won, you're being so naive.

13:21.425 --> 13:25.012
A businessman
should always prioritize margins.

13:28.307 --> 13:30.017
Gosh, I have a bad habit of meddling.

13:30.100 --> 13:31.352
I'm sure you'll do fine.

13:31.435 --> 13:33.521
Let's eat! Come on, sit.

14:01.757 --> 14:03.717
Mechoori.

14:04.593 --> 14:05.594
You're here.

14:05.678 --> 14:07.221
What's the occasion?

14:07.304 --> 14:08.639
You're all dressed up.

14:09.306 --> 14:10.975
And you invited me to a fancy restaurant.

14:11.559 --> 14:12.560
Sit down.

14:13.143 --> 14:14.687
No way…

14:16.480 --> 14:17.982
It can't be, right?

14:20.526 --> 14:22.027
I'm making a proposal.

14:22.111 --> 14:23.737
-To you.
-Wait.

14:25.239 --> 14:27.825
Hey, you should've given me a hint.

14:27.908 --> 14:30.995
Then I would've dressed up a bit too.

14:31.078 --> 14:32.538
I thought there was no way…

14:32.621 --> 14:34.123
You mean it?

14:48.304 --> 14:50.764
I'm making a product listing proposal,

14:50.848 --> 14:52.266
Ms. Dam Ye-jin.

14:54.643 --> 14:55.644
Product listing?

15:01.108 --> 15:02.109
GOJEUNEOK BIO CREAM

15:02.192 --> 15:04.111
DAM YE-JIN'S ONLY1,
PRODUCT PLACEMENT PROPOSAL

15:06.363 --> 15:07.740
Without you,

15:07.823 --> 15:10.367
I wouldn't even have started
developing this cream.

15:12.953 --> 15:14.747
Will you join me in finishing

15:15.581 --> 15:16.832
this project?

15:20.586 --> 15:23.047
Keep doubting me, and keep me on my toes.

15:24.465 --> 15:25.966
If I'm working with you,

15:27.051 --> 15:29.219
I won't feel worried.

15:52.993 --> 15:54.370
GOJEUNEOK BIO

16:42.918 --> 16:43.961
What are you looking for?

16:44.670 --> 16:45.713
I need to check something.

16:47.297 --> 16:49.883
You're not checking all of this, are you?

16:49.967 --> 16:52.511
I have no choice.
I have to look through everything.

16:53.637 --> 16:55.097
Mechoori.

16:55.180 --> 16:57.558
Let me give you a tip.

17:02.479 --> 17:03.522
Here.

17:03.605 --> 17:04.898
Explain what you're looking for.

17:08.736 --> 17:11.321
I'm looking for data
on the antimicrobial effects

17:11.405 --> 17:12.906
of major medicinal mushroom extracts

17:12.990 --> 17:14.867
studied by Seohan University's
research team.

17:15.868 --> 17:16.910
The paper you mentioned

17:16.994 --> 17:20.164
is part of the research on ingredients
that are effective and safe

17:20.247 --> 17:22.041
for sensitive skin.

17:22.124 --> 17:23.625
The antimicrobial test results

17:23.709 --> 17:26.628
against five microorganisms
that cause skin diseases

17:26.712 --> 17:30.966
showed an MIC of 19.72 µg/mL.

17:31.967 --> 17:36.013
Honestly, I was pleased
with the seventh sample too.

17:36.096 --> 17:37.639
I think we're finally getting there.

17:37.723 --> 17:39.516
-We can't be sure yet.
-We can't be sure yet.

17:44.521 --> 17:45.606
All right.

17:45.689 --> 17:47.900
Let's keep up this energy and continue.

17:47.983 --> 17:49.818
-Let's do this.
-Let's do this.

17:49.902 --> 17:52.946
You know, everything's fine, but…

17:55.074 --> 17:56.533
That's the scariest phrase.

17:58.911 --> 18:02.539
The smell of this white flower
noori mushroom bothers me a bit.

18:02.623 --> 18:05.918
A distinct fragrance
leads to mixed reactions,

18:06.001 --> 18:07.544
and that affects sales directly.

18:07.628 --> 18:10.631
Are you suggesting we add
synthetic fragrance just for sales?

18:10.714 --> 18:13.217
I'm talking about market viability.

18:13.300 --> 18:15.552
We want as many people as possible

18:15.636 --> 18:17.971
to use Gojeuneok's cream
and benefit from it, right?

18:18.055 --> 18:21.350
The scent is a matter of preference.
There isn't a right answer.

18:21.433 --> 18:22.810
Still…

18:22.893 --> 18:27.606
How many people would actually
say they like this smell?

18:31.401 --> 18:34.488
I believe we can effectively portray
Gojeuneok's natural concept--

18:34.571 --> 18:37.282
If that's your purpose,
it will be better to use

18:37.366 --> 18:39.868
citrus, marine, or woody scents
that are widely popular.

18:40.828 --> 18:42.621
Why don't we discuss what's better--

18:42.704 --> 18:43.997
Ms. Dam Ye-jin!

18:48.919 --> 18:52.923
I'm the developer of this cream,
and I know what's best for it.

18:53.799 --> 18:55.551
Mr. Lee Hae-seok.

18:56.468 --> 18:59.346
I'm just suggesting making another reason
for the customers to buy this.

18:59.429 --> 19:02.474
Why would luxury brands add
synthetic fragrances to their products?

19:02.558 --> 19:05.644
The scent itself
provides comfort and satisfaction.

19:05.727 --> 19:07.604
Once they experience this cream's effects,

19:07.688 --> 19:11.191
they'll end up liking this scent
that you hate so much.

19:13.485 --> 19:17.656
Mr. Lee, isn't this a meeting
to exchange feedback?

19:17.739 --> 19:20.033
It seems like you're not open
to any feedback at all.

19:20.117 --> 19:23.203
Ms. Dam, I would like to accept feedback
if it helps our product.

19:23.287 --> 19:24.454
Is this not helpful?

19:24.538 --> 19:25.539
I'm not sure.

19:28.709 --> 19:29.626
Let's take a break.

19:29.710 --> 19:31.420
Let's resume in 15 minutes.

19:45.475 --> 19:47.603
Will we really be able to sell this cream?

19:48.520 --> 19:50.480
Something's bound to happen
between those two.

19:50.564 --> 19:52.399
Then what about our broadcast?

19:55.360 --> 19:57.404
Geez.

20:04.328 --> 20:05.329
He's alone.

20:05.412 --> 20:07.164
They must have gotten into a fight!

20:07.748 --> 20:08.874
Where's Dam Ye-jin?

20:12.377 --> 20:14.463
I think she's with him.

20:14.546 --> 20:15.380
What?

20:23.013 --> 20:25.432
Hey, can't you…

20:26.058 --> 20:28.101
speak a bit more gently?

20:30.395 --> 20:31.521
I'll be more careful.

20:31.605 --> 20:33.190
That is a warning.

20:34.983 --> 20:36.902
We were worried for nothing.

20:37.778 --> 20:38.946
Let's go.

20:40.322 --> 20:42.199
-Honey potato!
-Cherry tomato!

20:42.282 --> 20:44.451
Cherry tomato's on a break.

20:44.534 --> 20:45.869
-Really?
-Did you have lunch?

20:45.953 --> 20:46.995
Of course.

20:47.079 --> 20:49.373
-What did you have?
-I had noodles.

20:56.380 --> 20:58.090
The texture is the same…

20:59.716 --> 21:01.677
And that funky smell too.

21:03.262 --> 21:04.263
Mr. Lee.

21:04.930 --> 21:07.599
The pilot test matches the sample.

21:09.518 --> 21:12.312
ASSESSMENT
PASS

21:17.192 --> 21:19.027
Great job.

21:20.028 --> 21:21.697
Good job.

21:22.406 --> 21:24.032
Great job.

21:24.116 --> 21:25.617
Have you decided on the name?

21:26.118 --> 21:29.121
We should finalize the name
before we go into production.

21:29.663 --> 21:31.665
I'm going to ask a naming specialist.

21:33.208 --> 21:34.418
Did you really clean it?

21:34.501 --> 21:36.628
-I did.
-Are you sure?

21:36.712 --> 21:38.255
I'm telling you, I did.

21:38.338 --> 21:39.840
No way. It's the same as yesterday.

21:39.923 --> 21:40.882
I did.

21:40.966 --> 21:42.592
-Just go.
-Som-yi.

21:42.676 --> 21:44.219
Mechoori.

21:44.303 --> 21:46.221
You're back from school?

21:48.640 --> 21:50.851
Som-yi, look.

21:53.979 --> 21:54.980
What is it?

21:56.356 --> 21:58.066
I made this cream.

21:58.150 --> 21:59.901
Wow, really?

21:59.985 --> 22:01.528
What's it made of?

22:02.529 --> 22:04.865
You know the white flower
noori mushroom, right?

22:04.948 --> 22:06.616
That and some other stuff.

22:07.409 --> 22:08.410
Som-yi.

22:09.202 --> 22:11.621
What should I name it?

22:12.122 --> 22:14.041
I'd like you to decide.

22:14.124 --> 22:15.417
The name?

22:18.128 --> 22:19.087
Noori Cream.

22:20.005 --> 22:20.839
Noori Cream?

22:21.840 --> 22:24.301
Hey, that's so tacky.

22:25.302 --> 22:29.348
I learned in school that "noori"
means "the whole world."

22:29.431 --> 22:30.515
It could mean

22:30.599 --> 22:33.060
that the whole world
will end up using this cream.

22:33.143 --> 22:34.728
Isn't that awesome?

22:37.898 --> 22:38.982
Noori Cream.

22:40.067 --> 22:41.068
I like it.

22:41.860 --> 22:43.028
See?

22:43.111 --> 22:44.738
Mechoori, can I use this?

22:50.160 --> 22:52.037
Of course. We can use it together.

22:52.120 --> 22:53.121
No.

22:53.205 --> 22:54.081
It's mine.

22:54.164 --> 22:56.958
I'll try this after I wash my face.

23:01.129 --> 23:02.839
Noori Cream is going to be a huge hit.

23:02.923 --> 23:04.424
It made that lazyhead wash her face.

23:07.385 --> 23:08.804
Right, Jin-yi…

23:11.431 --> 23:12.599
I was asked to give you this.

23:13.600 --> 23:14.601
By who?

23:19.940 --> 23:23.568
HIT's open recruitment deadline
is midnight today.

23:23.652 --> 23:26.905
I really hope you seize this chance
to show your talent.

23:29.741 --> 23:31.409
How long are you going to stay like that?

23:32.035 --> 23:34.287
I've been so excited for this moment.

23:34.371 --> 23:35.914
I want it to be a surprise.

23:38.250 --> 23:39.167
What was that?

23:39.793 --> 23:40.669
Hang on.

23:42.629 --> 23:43.463
All right.

23:48.176 --> 23:49.886
Are we here now? Can I open my eyes?

23:49.970 --> 23:51.429
Just a bit more.

23:52.722 --> 23:53.932
Now?

23:54.683 --> 23:56.143
Turn around here.

23:56.226 --> 23:58.019
Give me a countdown. Come on.

23:58.979 --> 23:59.980
Three, two--

24:04.901 --> 24:05.902
It's you.

24:07.112 --> 24:08.780
I was desperate to see you.

24:08.864 --> 24:11.241
Wow, you look so cool.

24:11.324 --> 24:12.367
Are you that happy?

24:12.450 --> 24:14.119
Isn't it obvious?

24:15.620 --> 24:16.496
Are you crying?

24:17.831 --> 24:19.166
Why would you cry over this?

24:19.249 --> 24:20.333
How could I not?

24:20.417 --> 24:22.085
You worked so hard to make this.

24:22.169 --> 24:24.045
Of course, I'd cry.

24:28.508 --> 24:29.885
You did an amazing job.

24:30.594 --> 24:32.012
I knew you could do it.

24:32.095 --> 24:33.430
Thank you

24:33.513 --> 24:34.890
for encouraging me every day.

24:36.141 --> 24:37.601
That kept me going.

24:48.820 --> 24:49.988
Come in.

24:51.281 --> 24:52.157
Director.

24:53.325 --> 24:54.201
Hey.

24:57.162 --> 24:58.330
You've waited a long time.

24:58.413 --> 25:01.249
I brought my first item
for Dam Ye-jin's Only1.

25:03.585 --> 25:05.128
GOJEUNEOK BIO REGENERATIVE CREAM

25:05.212 --> 25:06.087
Gojeuneok Bio…

25:07.631 --> 25:09.716
The raw material company
for La Fin Essence?

25:09.799 --> 25:13.011
Yes. And that meticulous company
made their first cosmetic product.

25:14.387 --> 25:15.805
Are you confident about this?

25:15.889 --> 25:16.723
Absolutely.

25:23.063 --> 25:23.980
Great job.

25:26.399 --> 25:27.609
Thanks.

25:30.111 --> 25:31.071
All right.

25:32.364 --> 25:35.200
You've all put in so much work
for our Noori Cream.

25:39.829 --> 25:41.915
Do you know what my credit card

25:41.998 --> 25:44.251
and you have in common?

25:44.334 --> 25:45.710
-No.
-What is it?

25:45.794 --> 25:47.337
There is no limit.

25:48.463 --> 25:49.631
That's awesome!

25:50.840 --> 25:53.343
Eat as much as you want,
and make sure to get drunk.

25:53.426 --> 25:54.427
For Noori Cream!

25:54.970 --> 25:56.638
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

26:03.436 --> 26:05.188
What are you doing? That's alcohol.

26:05.272 --> 26:07.274
I can drink now,

26:07.357 --> 26:08.775
thanks to someone.

26:12.529 --> 26:13.989
Let's just eat.

26:14.072 --> 26:16.366
Mechoori, this is really tasty.

26:16.449 --> 26:17.492
Try it.

26:17.575 --> 26:18.702
You should eat.

26:19.911 --> 26:22.330
-Go on, try it first.
-Only if you eat first.

26:23.039 --> 26:25.667
Gosh. Well, then…

26:25.750 --> 26:27.502
-Excuse me.
-My gosh.

26:28.336 --> 26:29.337
Here, eat this first.

26:29.421 --> 26:31.589
I picked the wrong seat.

26:35.552 --> 26:36.553
Isn't it good?

26:38.596 --> 26:40.140
Potatoes.

26:42.267 --> 26:44.102
I miss my potato.

26:56.406 --> 26:59.451
Can I have another bottle of beer?

27:00.160 --> 27:01.578
That's enough.

27:01.661 --> 27:03.747
Go home.

27:05.957 --> 27:07.959
Hey, cherry tomato.

27:08.043 --> 27:09.627
Honey potato.

27:09.711 --> 27:10.879
What are you doing here?

27:12.088 --> 27:13.089
You said you miss me.

27:14.674 --> 27:17.594
You came all the way here
just because I said that?

27:19.012 --> 27:21.890
If I tell you to die,
would you really die for me?

27:28.396 --> 27:29.356
You're so cute.

27:30.065 --> 27:31.274
Park Kwang-mo, you're so cute.

27:32.317 --> 27:33.318
So cute.

27:33.401 --> 27:36.363
You're so, so, so adorable.

27:36.446 --> 27:37.739
Adorable?

27:39.366 --> 27:42.869
I'm not just adorable, you know.

27:50.210 --> 27:51.586
You… You got that?

28:20.865 --> 28:27.580
-So cute!
-So cute!

28:45.640 --> 28:46.474
Mr. Seo.

28:56.067 --> 29:00.363
It always seems to rain when I meet you.

29:01.406 --> 29:02.907
Right?

29:03.533 --> 29:07.036
But the weather is usually nice
when I go somewhere.

29:07.662 --> 29:10.915
I think you're the one
who's summoning the rain.

29:16.755 --> 29:19.799
Why didn't you come that day?

29:23.803 --> 29:25.054
Well…

29:25.138 --> 29:26.973
Since it's raining,

29:28.224 --> 29:30.310
this seems like
an appropriate moment to ask.

29:35.523 --> 29:37.859
If you believe in fate,

29:37.942 --> 29:41.488
why don't we just meet here tomorrow?

29:41.571 --> 29:43.114
I wanted to believe in fate.

29:43.907 --> 29:44.908
It had been

29:46.117 --> 29:48.077
a long time since anyone

29:49.120 --> 29:50.914
looked at me with such sparkling eyes.

29:51.664 --> 29:53.583
I should be there by 12:00 p.m.,

29:54.793 --> 29:56.461
so I should wake up at 10:00 a.m.

29:57.128 --> 29:59.214
No, I'll get up at 9:30 a.m.

30:08.932 --> 30:13.561
I wanted to get a good night's sleep
and show up looking refreshed…

30:21.694 --> 30:23.905
But when I woke up, it was evening.

30:25.490 --> 30:29.744
The new meds I was prescribed
didn't agree with me.

30:49.430 --> 30:50.431
I see.

30:54.143 --> 30:56.062
Though it's all in the past,

30:56.938 --> 31:00.024
I don't want to dismiss
the time I spent with you.

31:01.192 --> 31:02.819
I really had a great time.

31:03.862 --> 31:08.491
And those memories helped me
whenever things were tough.

31:10.869 --> 31:11.870
Thank you

31:12.537 --> 31:14.080
for cherishing those memories.

31:15.707 --> 31:17.667
The time I spent with you

31:18.418 --> 31:20.587
will be a valuable memory for me too.

31:21.880 --> 31:26.050
Thanks to your sincerity
and dedication to your work,

31:27.552 --> 31:29.721
I figured out
what sort of path I want to take.

31:30.471 --> 31:31.472
Maybe that's why…

31:32.932 --> 31:35.143
the Eric Seo I saw while working

31:35.226 --> 31:38.396
was much cooler than the man
three years ago under that umbrella.

31:39.480 --> 31:40.481
Really?

31:45.111 --> 31:48.072
Do you know the word "blindly"?

31:50.116 --> 31:53.661
It means doing something
without any plans or thoughts.

31:55.747 --> 31:56.748
That sounds nice.

31:56.831 --> 32:00.126
But that's actually pretty difficult.

32:00.209 --> 32:03.463
So, how about walking blindly with me?

32:03.546 --> 32:05.423
I'll give you a relaxing tour.

32:05.506 --> 32:06.799
Let's go, stranger.

32:27.612 --> 32:28.696
DAM YE-JIN'S ONLY1

32:31.491 --> 32:35.161
We're doing a lucky draw event
where you can win various rewards

32:35.244 --> 32:38.748
from the Noori Cream to a discount code
you can use for the launch broadcast.

32:38.831 --> 32:40.750
This is why you're our ace host.

32:41.626 --> 32:45.713
The Noori Cream is the hottest item
among the merchandisers right now.

32:45.797 --> 32:49.550
Everyone was wondering how you found
such a precious gem

32:49.634 --> 32:51.636
-and was praising you--
-Mr. Hwang.

32:52.720 --> 32:54.889
You should give more precise details.

32:54.973 --> 32:56.641
How exactly did they praise me?

32:56.724 --> 32:59.894
Right. The Noori Cream
pre-release trial event.

33:00.478 --> 33:01.521
Did you know

33:01.604 --> 33:04.774
we were selecting 30 people,
but there were over 500 applicants?

33:04.857 --> 33:08.111
It was so tough doing the draw.

33:08.194 --> 33:09.612
When can we see the reviews?

33:09.696 --> 33:10.530
In two weeks.

33:10.613 --> 33:13.241
I'll organize all the reviews
when they're out

33:13.324 --> 33:14.784
and share them with you.

33:14.867 --> 33:17.495
We have to use the reviews
for our inserts,

33:17.578 --> 33:19.163
so make sure to get all the photos.

33:25.503 --> 33:28.506
I brought salt bread made
with Guérande sea salt from France…

33:28.589 --> 33:30.925
And you're already drinking coffee.

33:31.801 --> 33:33.344
Mr. Cha,

33:34.929 --> 33:36.764
you're really photogenic.

33:38.099 --> 33:38.933
What?

33:39.600 --> 33:40.435
Bring them over.

33:50.778 --> 33:52.822
He passed the secretary interview
with these photos.

33:52.905 --> 33:53.823
Impressive, right?

33:59.120 --> 34:00.580
Eat that yourself.

34:01.122 --> 34:02.290
You'll need it.

34:15.053 --> 34:16.054
Did you play basketball?

34:19.640 --> 34:20.475
I'm moving in.

34:22.769 --> 34:24.103
Block properly.

34:29.859 --> 34:30.902
What?

34:30.985 --> 34:32.236
-That young man…
-Isn't he cold?

34:35.531 --> 34:37.158
-I'm not cold…
-Mr. Cha!

34:37.241 --> 34:38.701
What happened?

34:38.785 --> 34:39.619
I'm sorry.

34:39.702 --> 34:40.953
I got caught.

34:41.037 --> 34:42.288
What…

34:42.371 --> 34:43.498
Did you get hit?

34:43.998 --> 34:45.416
I'm fine.

34:45.500 --> 34:47.001
No, you're not.

34:47.085 --> 34:51.631
Still, I managed to pull one over on them.

35:05.186 --> 35:06.020
Right.

35:06.104 --> 35:10.149
I'll find something in there, even if
I have to look through it all night.

35:11.901 --> 35:15.571
By the way, it'll be hard
tracking Ms. Michelle's movements now.

35:15.655 --> 35:16.823
What do we do?

35:20.118 --> 35:22.703
GOJEUNEOK BIO

35:26.124 --> 35:27.125
Mr. Lee.

35:27.208 --> 35:28.459
Yes?

35:29.502 --> 35:30.920
There's something you should see.

35:44.475 --> 35:46.102
The person claiming to be the victim

35:46.185 --> 35:48.062
is a beauty creator called Sensitive Assi.

35:48.646 --> 35:50.648
She has an inflammatory skin condition.

35:51.274 --> 35:53.901
Since she's a well-known creator
and the content's pretty intense,

35:53.985 --> 35:56.487
it's spreading quickly
on social media and online communities.

35:56.571 --> 35:58.281
It's just her claim.

35:59.031 --> 36:00.992
She could've eaten something
that caused it.

36:01.075 --> 36:03.703
We ran this through numerous testing labs.

36:03.786 --> 36:05.788
It can't be true.

36:07.540 --> 36:09.167
Let me make a call.

36:11.085 --> 36:12.253
MECHOORI

36:13.546 --> 36:14.547
Hello?

36:14.630 --> 36:17.049
Ms. Dam, you saw the post, right?

36:17.133 --> 36:18.801
We're looking into this matter right now.

36:18.885 --> 36:20.303
CEO LEE HAE-SEOK

36:25.683 --> 36:27.685
I'll call you again later.

36:28.311 --> 36:29.896
Is something going on?

36:30.688 --> 36:31.939
Mechoori.

36:33.816 --> 36:36.652
ANOTHER GOOD MORNING CREAM INCIDENT?
RESEARCHER RETURNS WITHOUT REMORSE

36:51.375 --> 36:52.376
DEOKPUNG HID LEE HAE-SEOK

36:52.460 --> 36:56.505
Mechoori, a bunch of people
stormed in last night

36:56.589 --> 36:59.133
and made a total mess in the village.

36:59.217 --> 37:00.384
What should we do?

37:00.468 --> 37:02.011
I thought you should know, at least.

37:02.094 --> 37:03.304
Goodness.

37:03.387 --> 37:05.181
TAKE RESPONSIBILITY
CRIMINAL LEE HAE-SEOK OUT

37:05.264 --> 37:06.599
What do I do?

37:13.189 --> 37:14.232
This is ridiculous.

37:14.315 --> 37:15.441
Over there.

37:15.524 --> 37:16.984
Where? Let's hurry.

37:17.652 --> 37:18.611
This is nonsense.

37:21.364 --> 37:23.074
WHAT YOU MADE IS POISON, NOT CREAM

37:23.157 --> 37:24.325
"Poison, not cream"?

37:25.243 --> 37:26.452
Jin-yi, who are they?

37:26.535 --> 37:27.745
Let's go inside.

37:27.828 --> 37:29.747
Why? They're heading to Mechoori's house.

37:29.830 --> 37:32.208
Let's just go inside, all right?

37:39.966 --> 37:41.092
You'll hurt someone!

37:41.175 --> 37:43.302
Please, calm down and talk this out.

37:43.386 --> 37:44.595
Tell him to get out here!

37:44.679 --> 37:46.264
You all know him, don't you?

37:46.973 --> 37:49.016
Just talk it out. Please.

37:49.100 --> 37:49.934
He's here.

37:50.726 --> 37:51.560
That jerk's here.

37:55.189 --> 37:57.024
You're finally showing your face.

37:57.108 --> 37:59.485
You were hiding here all along
after ruining my kid's skin?

37:59.568 --> 38:02.071
Look at my face.

38:02.154 --> 38:03.864
You see what you did to me?

38:03.948 --> 38:05.908
Fix what you did!

38:05.992 --> 38:09.829
Fix my kid's face
and all our lives you ruined!

38:09.912 --> 38:11.956
This isn't going to solve anything!

38:12.039 --> 38:13.916
Talk this out! People will get hurt!

38:14.000 --> 38:14.959
Are you okay, Mechoori?

38:15.042 --> 38:18.713
Everyone, please calm down.
Let's talk this over, all right?

38:18.796 --> 38:20.881
My child can't even wear
short sleeves in summer

38:20.965 --> 38:22.174
or go to a swimming pool

38:22.258 --> 38:24.593
because of the cream he made!

38:25.886 --> 38:26.887
I'm sorry.

38:27.680 --> 38:28.556
Hey!

38:28.639 --> 38:31.600
"Sorry"? You try using
that cream, you jerk!

38:33.853 --> 38:34.854
Please, calm down!

38:34.937 --> 38:36.605
Move aside!

38:38.399 --> 38:39.692
Jong-il!

38:39.775 --> 38:40.943
Jong-il.

38:41.027 --> 38:42.570
-Are you hurt?
-Are you okay?

38:42.653 --> 38:44.697
You must've hurt your back. What do we do?

38:44.780 --> 38:46.782
Why did you have to butt in like that?

38:46.866 --> 38:48.367
Are you kidding me?

38:48.451 --> 38:49.744
Look here!

38:49.827 --> 38:52.496
This isn't the time
to be blaming each other!

38:53.080 --> 38:54.123
Get out.

38:54.206 --> 38:57.126
If you don't leave, I'm calling the cops.

38:57.209 --> 38:59.128
So get out! Leave!

39:00.129 --> 39:01.130
Let's go talk outside.

39:01.213 --> 39:02.173
Leave!

39:02.256 --> 39:04.550
-Get out. Out already!
-Come on!

39:04.633 --> 39:08.137
Choi Woo-su took responsibility
with his life. What about you?

39:08.637 --> 39:10.139
Are you all right?

39:11.015 --> 39:12.600
You asshole!

39:14.435 --> 39:15.686
You're a criminal.

39:16.896 --> 39:18.606
-Oh, gosh.
-Hurry up and leave!

39:18.689 --> 39:20.316
-Can you get up?
-Jong-il!

39:21.692 --> 39:24.278
Goodness. I don't think I can get up.

39:45.216 --> 39:50.429
NO CREAM SALES
CRIMINAL LEE HAE-SEOK OUT

40:09.323 --> 40:10.658
Be careful.

40:10.741 --> 40:11.784
My gosh.

40:11.867 --> 40:13.828
-I can't believe this!
-This is terrible.

40:15.955 --> 40:16.956
He must be hurt badly.

40:21.502 --> 40:24.338
Are you all right? Let's head inside.

40:25.506 --> 40:26.841
I'm sorry, ma'am.

40:27.550 --> 40:30.177
I'll clean up here.

40:35.433 --> 40:39.520
You must have a lot on your mind.
Just go inside, will you?

40:39.603 --> 40:43.983
Leave him be. He said he'll clean up.

40:45.234 --> 40:49.405
I'll take down the banner
at the community center.

40:49.488 --> 40:52.741
-Don't worry about that.
-You could get hurt too.

40:52.825 --> 40:56.579
Every house has been spray-painted.
Let's just go clean those.

40:56.662 --> 40:57.705
It's fine.

40:57.788 --> 41:02.168
This used to be a peaceful neighborhood!
How can this happen overnight?

41:02.251 --> 41:04.086
That's enough!

41:06.797 --> 41:08.132
I'm sorry.

41:09.967 --> 41:11.677
I'll sort things out as fast as I can

41:13.179 --> 41:15.139
and leave the village

41:15.806 --> 41:17.099
before I cause any more trouble.

41:27.735 --> 41:29.320
Why aren't you saying anything?

41:30.029 --> 41:32.573
How could you do this to him?

41:33.157 --> 41:35.034
How can you say that to us?

41:35.117 --> 41:37.953
You heard what they all said.

41:38.037 --> 41:41.415
Can you still take Mechoori's side
after hearing all that?

41:41.499 --> 41:42.708
Has…

41:43.834 --> 41:47.379
Has anyone here not received
Mechoori's help before?

41:47.463 --> 41:50.049
How can you be so ungrateful?

41:50.132 --> 41:51.759
You're the one who's being cold.

41:52.635 --> 41:57.139
We've been neighbors for over 30 years,
and you're putting him before us?

41:57.223 --> 42:01.268
Who is he to you?

42:01.352 --> 42:02.728
That's not what I meant.

42:02.811 --> 42:04.647
That's not it.

42:04.730 --> 42:08.108
For the first time,
let me ask you a favor.

42:10.486 --> 42:13.781
He's like my son.

42:13.864 --> 42:17.326
He's like the child I buried in my heart.

42:18.827 --> 42:23.123
The child I buried in my heart.

42:23.832 --> 42:26.794
He's like my own child.

42:27.670 --> 42:30.422
He's like my son.

42:42.518 --> 42:43.686
Bong-chan…

42:44.603 --> 42:46.897
Come home by dinnertime.
You'll ruin your health.

42:46.981 --> 42:48.941
I had a son.

42:49.650 --> 42:52.403
I did nothing for him,

42:52.486 --> 42:56.407
but he was a kind son
who always worried about me.

42:56.490 --> 43:00.160
What do we do?

43:00.244 --> 43:04.790
The boat Bong-chan was on went over.

43:06.417 --> 43:10.546
That day was my son's birthday.

43:13.591 --> 43:16.760
I couldn't even cook
warm soup for him on his birthdays.

43:18.012 --> 43:22.850
I should have made him some…

43:24.351 --> 43:25.352
Bong-chan…

43:27.521 --> 43:30.733
While living with regret,

43:30.816 --> 43:34.069
I saw Mechoori one day

43:35.237 --> 43:37.990
as I was on my way to visit Bong-chan.

43:46.999 --> 43:49.960
Excuse me. Hey.

43:51.795 --> 43:52.838
Young man.

43:52.921 --> 43:55.174
It's cold out here.

43:55.924 --> 43:59.261
Come on, let's go inside. It's cold.

44:03.015 --> 44:04.975
Mechoori.

44:06.226 --> 44:07.936
Have some potatoes.

44:08.020 --> 44:11.398
After feeding him
and spending time with him,

44:12.816 --> 44:18.238
I could see how foolishly kind he was,
just like my son.

44:20.824 --> 44:23.243
But that foolishness

44:24.036 --> 44:28.040
blew a warm spring breeze through my heart

44:29.166 --> 44:31.585
and our entire village.

44:37.007 --> 44:39.051
The heavens are so cruel.

44:40.386 --> 44:43.764
I wondered why they left me
all alone without my son,

44:45.933 --> 44:48.268
but I guess I was left here

44:49.770 --> 44:51.397
to hold your hand.

45:21.885 --> 45:23.637
Great work today.

45:32.020 --> 45:34.231
-What happened?
-Oh, gosh!

45:34.314 --> 45:35.858
So what did you do?

45:35.941 --> 45:36.984
So then, you know…

45:37.067 --> 45:39.361
It looked like a cow had licked it.

45:39.445 --> 45:41.780
-I really can't work with them.
-Me either.

45:41.864 --> 45:43.574
Ms. Ji Yun-ji.

45:45.659 --> 45:46.910
Congratulations on selling out.

45:47.870 --> 45:49.204
Can I talk to you for a minute?

45:50.289 --> 45:51.415
Let's go.

46:07.306 --> 46:09.141
You shouldn't come here.

46:09.683 --> 46:11.810
I wanted to treat you to something nice.

46:13.770 --> 46:15.647
The pre-release tester list
for Noori Cream

46:16.440 --> 46:18.400
was a great help.

46:20.235 --> 46:21.695
I'm done then, right?

46:22.613 --> 46:24.823
Don't ever visit me or contact me again.

46:26.033 --> 46:27.409
You really think…

46:29.119 --> 46:30.787
you can get off

46:31.413 --> 46:33.790
that easy, Ms. Ji?

46:33.874 --> 46:36.293
Mr. Son!

46:36.376 --> 46:40.255
The public reaction is getting pretty bad.
This should be enough.

46:40.339 --> 46:42.716
Who would buy the Noori Cream?

46:42.799 --> 46:46.929
Noori Cream was never my target, Ms. Ji.

46:47.012 --> 46:49.389
It was someone who still
hasn't learned his lesson

46:49.473 --> 46:51.225
after what happened five years ago.

46:52.976 --> 46:54.186
Lee Hae-seok.

46:55.395 --> 46:57.189
I have to finish him this time.

47:01.985 --> 47:03.862
What's the urgent news?

47:03.946 --> 47:07.574
I found out who Ms. Michelle
was meeting in secret.

47:11.995 --> 47:13.956
Who is this guy?

47:20.963 --> 47:22.923
Why would Chang-ho…

47:23.006 --> 47:25.842
Do you have any ideas as to why my sister

47:25.926 --> 47:27.386
would be meeting Son Chang-ho?

47:30.722 --> 47:32.140
One thing for sure

47:32.224 --> 47:35.811
is that there is no clear reason
why H.O. Cosmetics is buying

47:35.894 --> 47:37.771
Gojeuneok Bio's raw material.

47:37.854 --> 47:41.191
L'Étoile is currently planning
to enter the Asian market.

47:41.733 --> 47:42.734
But La Fin Essence

47:43.485 --> 47:45.612
was listed as a main product.

47:46.989 --> 47:48.532
La Fin Essence?

47:48.615 --> 47:50.492
Yes. Isn't that strange?

47:51.285 --> 47:54.621
They already used up
Gojeuneok Bio's materials a long time ago.

48:13.515 --> 48:16.184
UNITED IN PASSION,
NUAMER'S VISION COMES TO LIFE

48:18.979 --> 48:21.523
H.O. COSMETICS CLIENT LIST

48:27.988 --> 48:29.448
Who are you?

48:31.074 --> 48:32.075
Leave.

48:32.159 --> 48:33.660
We closed a long time ago.

48:34.870 --> 48:36.246
Do you know

48:36.955 --> 48:38.957
Son Chang-ho, by any chance?

48:41.376 --> 48:42.377
Who?

48:42.961 --> 48:45.631
I heard H.O. Cosmetics
and Nuamer signed an MoU

48:45.714 --> 48:48.300
and were co-developing products
until last year.

48:48.383 --> 48:52.220
All that talk about research,
collaboration, boosting technology…

48:53.138 --> 48:54.723
He was quite the smooth talker.

48:54.806 --> 48:58.268
We fell for it and signed the deal,

48:58.352 --> 49:00.687
and had all our core technology stolen.

49:00.771 --> 49:02.856
What about patents?
Did you not register any?

49:02.939 --> 49:08.528
How can small businesses like us
handle all those procedures and costs?

49:09.071 --> 49:12.574
Still, you must have your R&amp;D data
to be able to prove it.

49:12.658 --> 49:15.619
We tried every lawsuit we could think of,

49:15.702 --> 49:17.829
but we got hit with a countersuit
and lost everything.

49:17.913 --> 49:20.832
They'd already prepared
their own R&amp;D data.

49:21.416 --> 49:24.127
But I heard H.O. Cosmetics
has their own R&amp;D center

49:24.211 --> 49:26.046
and invests quite aggressively as well.

49:26.129 --> 49:27.506
Says who?

49:28.090 --> 49:31.218
They have no intention
of spending money on their products.

49:31.301 --> 49:34.680
They copied our new product
and switched the materials to cheap ones,

49:34.763 --> 49:37.474
then sold them at an even higher price.

49:37.557 --> 49:39.059
Hang on.

49:39.142 --> 49:40.811
What did you just say?

49:41.728 --> 49:43.105
They switched the materials?

49:43.188 --> 49:44.606
Yes.

49:44.690 --> 49:46.900
He said there was no need
for expensive materials

49:46.983 --> 49:49.861
and wanted to switch to cheaper ones
to improve margins.

49:50.612 --> 49:53.448
A businessman
should always prioritize margins.

49:53.532 --> 49:56.576
Woo-su switched the raw materials.

50:06.586 --> 50:09.297
You must have gotten mixed up
in Son Chang-ho's scheme as well.

50:09.798 --> 50:11.049
Be careful.

50:11.133 --> 50:12.592
If things don't go his way,

50:12.676 --> 50:14.928
he'll resort to anything, even violence.

50:24.312 --> 50:25.480
Ms. Moon.

50:26.940 --> 50:27.774
You're closed.

50:29.067 --> 50:31.820
Yes. I already turned off
all the machines.

50:31.903 --> 50:33.155
I see…

50:33.905 --> 50:36.283
I wanted a cup of your cappuccino.

50:37.743 --> 50:38.910
Too bad.

50:39.995 --> 50:41.705
I'll come back next time, then.

50:44.499 --> 50:45.500
Wait…

50:46.668 --> 50:50.505
I do have some alcohol, though.

51:00.849 --> 51:01.683
This is good.

51:05.896 --> 51:07.689
Is something going on?

51:07.773 --> 51:10.650
You're not acting cheesy today.

51:14.321 --> 51:15.947
Ms. Moon.

51:16.615 --> 51:20.243
Have you ever seen a hidden side
to someone close to you?

51:22.078 --> 51:25.957
I'm not even sure
who I've been spending time with,

51:27.751 --> 51:31.338
or whether I just never knew
who they really were.

51:31.922 --> 51:33.215
It's complicated.

51:34.841 --> 51:36.051
It's not complicated.

51:37.511 --> 51:39.095
The one who deceived you is bad,

51:40.180 --> 51:41.306
and the one who got fooled

51:42.891 --> 51:44.309
is just a victim.

51:49.523 --> 51:51.441
Don't feel upset over a bad person.

51:52.984 --> 51:53.985
That jerk

51:55.779 --> 51:58.031
has no clue

51:59.241 --> 52:00.909
how much you're suffering anyway.

52:02.869 --> 52:04.037
That jerk is the guy

52:05.372 --> 52:07.415
who wore the same watch as me, right?

52:13.588 --> 52:14.589
Yes.

52:37.904 --> 52:39.072
I…

52:40.031 --> 52:42.742
feel better if I have something warm
when I'm upset.

52:44.661 --> 52:45.745
Wait just a moment.

52:45.829 --> 52:48.290
I'll make you a warm cup of cappuccino.

53:10.854 --> 53:14.065
CANCEL THE LAUNCH BROADCAST
THIS IS GARBAGE

53:19.112 --> 53:21.031
MECHOORI

53:24.117 --> 53:26.453
HIT HWANG KI-HONG MD

53:27.537 --> 53:28.663
Mr. Hwang.

53:30.248 --> 53:31.249
Ms. Dam.

53:31.917 --> 53:34.044
The influencer Sensitive Assi…
Her name's Chu Min-a,

53:34.127 --> 53:36.630
and she was a pre-release tester.

53:36.713 --> 53:39.382
And all six people who made
the claims were testers too.

53:39.466 --> 53:41.092
Doesn't this seem strange?

53:41.176 --> 53:43.720
We distributed tons of samples
at our pop-up,

53:43.803 --> 53:46.681
but none of them had any issues with it.

53:46.765 --> 53:50.435
Then let's check the cream
that was given to the testers

53:50.518 --> 53:51.519
and run tests again.

53:53.480 --> 53:56.566
These are the results I just got.

53:58.944 --> 54:00.779
TEST RESULTS
PASS

54:00.862 --> 54:02.906
There's nothing wrong with the cream.

54:08.411 --> 54:09.829
Darn it.

54:11.790 --> 54:14.834
How can't a single one of them pick up?

54:14.918 --> 54:16.378
Are they all in this together?

54:16.461 --> 54:18.046
It seems like reverse viral marketing.

54:18.129 --> 54:20.799
We have to hurry and announce
that there aren't any issues.

54:21.466 --> 54:22.968
I know,

54:23.051 --> 54:26.513
but would anyone believe us
if we just say there's nothing wrong?

54:35.146 --> 54:36.398
Hello?

54:36.481 --> 54:38.149
It's me, Jin-yi.

54:40.694 --> 54:41.695
Jin-yi?

54:41.778 --> 54:43.613
Come on.

54:44.406 --> 54:46.241
I want to help Mechoori.

54:49.035 --> 54:52.914
My sister's skin
is practically litmus paper.

54:52.998 --> 54:54.749
She has chronic atopic dermatitis,

54:54.833 --> 54:56.835
so her skin reacts immediately

54:56.918 --> 54:58.420
to the slightest irritation.

54:59.004 --> 55:01.756
She's been using
this Noori Cream sample every day,

55:01.840 --> 55:04.050
but she hasn't shown any signs
of irritation.

55:04.134 --> 55:05.677
I FEEL RELIEVED SEEING THIS

55:05.760 --> 55:08.179
It doesn't feel itchy at all.

55:11.641 --> 55:15.311
This is the safety test report
we received from a testing lab

55:15.395 --> 55:17.564
designated by Korea's Ministry
of Food and Drug Safety.

55:17.647 --> 55:22.027
If you see the report here,
everything came back as "not detected."

55:22.610 --> 55:26.031
There wasn't a single substance
that was harmful.

55:34.706 --> 55:36.332
The thing you asked me to look into…

55:37.083 --> 55:39.461
The person who met with Ji Yun-ji…

55:39.544 --> 55:44.799
It was Son Chang-ho, the CEO
of H.O. Cosmetics, based in Thailand.

55:48.219 --> 55:49.721
THE USU, LEAD RESEARCHER

55:49.804 --> 55:51.598
There's one more thing.

55:53.725 --> 55:55.769
YUHAM CHILDREN'S PARK

55:55.852 --> 55:56.811
Seo-a!

55:57.771 --> 55:58.605
Climb up.

56:00.106 --> 56:01.775
Go on.

56:03.610 --> 56:06.029
To the side. Over there.

56:09.657 --> 56:10.825
Ms. Song.

56:11.701 --> 56:13.828
Oh, gosh. Ms. Song.

56:14.412 --> 56:15.455
How did you…

56:16.289 --> 56:20.418
I believe we have
a lot to talk about, Ms. Ji.

56:22.420 --> 56:25.298
Did you need something from me?

56:25.381 --> 56:27.884
How do you know Son Chang-ho?

56:29.511 --> 56:31.888
I heard you were supposed to do

56:32.680 --> 56:34.432
the Good Morning Cream broadcast.

56:35.725 --> 56:39.145
-Mom.
-Hey, Seo-a.

56:41.856 --> 56:46.194
I need to ask you
for a rather difficult favor.

56:46.778 --> 56:49.280
I have to protect my daughter too.

56:49.364 --> 56:51.116
Thank you so much, Jin-yi.

56:51.199 --> 56:54.744
It's nothing. I was able to muster up
my courage thanks to Som-yi.

56:54.828 --> 56:59.165
We should've mentioned that Mechoori
donates to the victims' group every month.

57:00.583 --> 57:03.086
I'm sure Mechoori
will be very grateful too.

57:03.169 --> 57:04.170
Ye-jin…

57:06.214 --> 57:09.342
Can I talk to you for a moment?

57:15.181 --> 57:16.766
Hae-seok.

57:17.934 --> 57:19.853
It's been such a long time.

57:19.936 --> 57:21.438
Yes, it's been a while.

57:21.521 --> 57:22.772
How have you been?

57:24.441 --> 57:26.151
I came to visit Woo-su.

57:57.640 --> 58:00.310
ARTICLE 3. UNIT PRICE AND ORDERS
418,000 WON PER KG

58:02.187 --> 58:04.355
ARTICLE 3. UNIT PRICE AND ORDERS
27,000 WON PER KG

58:24.584 --> 58:26.002
The home shopping host

58:27.712 --> 58:29.422
mentioned in gossip articles
five years ago

58:31.549 --> 58:33.259
about receiving a bribe…

58:37.430 --> 58:38.723
That was me.

58:41.059 --> 58:42.435
Are you a reporter?

58:42.519 --> 58:44.395
Are you trying to blackmail me with this?

58:45.188 --> 58:46.272
I'm not even a celebrity.

58:46.356 --> 58:48.441
What's so wrong with me
secretly having a child?

58:49.025 --> 58:49.901
Tell me!

58:50.693 --> 58:53.655
Calm down. I'm only here
to suggest we help each other.

58:54.322 --> 58:55.532
LISTING PROPOSAL

58:55.615 --> 58:57.200
I'm sure

58:57.283 --> 59:01.371
that you can easily get an item
on the list without an evaluation.

59:01.955 --> 59:05.625
If you list Good Morning Cream
on HIT's prime time slot,

59:06.584 --> 59:09.087
I'll give you money
with no strings attached.

59:11.381 --> 59:14.717
Just follow the proper procedures.

59:15.510 --> 59:16.928
Seo-a…

59:17.512 --> 59:20.348
needs her surgery, doesn't she?

59:25.812 --> 59:28.815
Chang-ho,
I'm asking you for the last time.

59:29.315 --> 59:31.234
Please reveal the truth.

59:32.360 --> 59:33.861
I won't leave you all alone.

59:33.945 --> 59:35.613
I'll take responsibility with you.

59:36.322 --> 59:38.616
I feel like I'm the one
who made you like this.

59:39.409 --> 59:40.535
I'm sorry.

59:42.120 --> 59:43.413
I'm sorry, Ye-jin.

59:44.163 --> 59:46.916
I shouldn't have done that to you

59:48.084 --> 59:50.837
just for my own sake.

59:55.592 --> 59:56.843
I know it's late,

59:58.469 --> 01:00:00.305
but I have something to give you.

01:00:10.231 --> 01:00:11.065
VOICE RECORDING

01:00:11.149 --> 01:00:12.275
It's all in there.

01:00:14.444 --> 01:00:16.321
It contains everything

01:00:17.697 --> 01:00:20.116
about how the Good Morning Cream
incident happened.

01:00:26.831 --> 01:00:28.374
CEO SON CHANG-HO

01:00:40.219 --> 01:00:42.513
Hae-seok, what brings you here?

01:00:49.812 --> 01:00:51.230
Explain this.

01:00:52.231 --> 01:00:54.233
What are you talking about?

01:00:57.320 --> 01:00:58.196
What is this?

01:00:58.279 --> 01:01:01.199
Don't ask. Just explain.

01:01:05.703 --> 01:01:07.830
You're the one who should explain.

01:01:08.498 --> 01:01:09.540
What's this about?

01:01:10.667 --> 01:01:12.085
Did you do this to Woo-su too?

01:01:16.589 --> 01:01:17.423
Hae-seok.

01:01:18.591 --> 01:01:21.052
You seem to be mistaken about something.

01:01:21.969 --> 01:01:23.888
Whatever it is,

01:01:23.971 --> 01:01:25.264
Woo-su will be upset

01:01:26.265 --> 01:01:29.143
seeing us having a conflict like this.

01:01:32.939 --> 01:01:36.734
Don't you dare say Woo-su's name
with that filthy mouth.

01:01:37.360 --> 01:01:39.320
Don't you get it, Hae-seok?

01:01:40.363 --> 01:01:42.115
You've been deceived by him too.

01:01:42.198 --> 01:01:44.242
That's the truth!

01:01:53.710 --> 01:01:55.294
Mr. Son!

01:01:55.378 --> 01:01:57.338
You said there was nothing wrong
with the product.

01:01:57.422 --> 01:01:58.631
Someone might see us.

01:01:58.715 --> 01:02:01.676
You said you used cheaper materials,
but there wouldn't be any issues.

01:02:03.553 --> 01:02:05.304
Are you questioning me right now?

01:02:06.347 --> 01:02:09.517
Ms. Ji, why are you suddenly
pretending to be naive?

01:02:10.309 --> 01:02:13.438
Did you really think there wouldn't be
any risks when you received the money?

01:02:14.147 --> 01:02:15.231
No,

01:02:15.314 --> 01:02:17.400
you handed the show
to your junior because you knew.

01:02:17.483 --> 01:02:18.317
Be honest.

01:02:19.235 --> 01:02:20.570
Did you really not know?

01:02:20.653 --> 01:02:22.196
Did you not?

01:02:26.033 --> 01:02:27.785
That's the truth.

01:02:30.830 --> 01:02:32.999
And that's why Woo-su died.

01:02:44.218 --> 01:02:45.219
Chang-ho.

01:02:46.262 --> 01:02:49.182
You said you'd take care of this

01:02:49.265 --> 01:02:51.309
when I was on a business trip
to Jeju Island, right?

01:02:52.393 --> 01:02:53.478
What are you talking about?

01:02:55.688 --> 01:02:57.398
When did I say that?

01:02:58.107 --> 01:03:01.486
Chang-ho, just be honest with me.

01:03:01.569 --> 01:03:03.446
Please. Just tell me.

01:03:05.406 --> 01:03:09.368
Woo-su, I know you're standing
on the edge of a cliff right now,

01:03:10.286 --> 01:03:11.662
but you shouldn't do this.

01:03:13.581 --> 01:03:16.042
You're the one who switched
the material, you jerk!

01:03:21.005 --> 01:03:22.507
Do you have proof?

01:03:25.384 --> 01:03:26.469
You…

01:03:27.261 --> 01:03:28.095
You didn't, right?

01:03:29.931 --> 01:03:31.182
Tell me it wasn't you!

01:03:31.766 --> 01:03:33.768
It wasn't, right? Tell me!

01:03:34.268 --> 01:03:35.436
It wasn't you, was it?

01:03:37.772 --> 01:03:38.981
How could you…

01:03:40.107 --> 01:03:42.193
Please tell me it wasn't you!

01:03:44.195 --> 01:03:46.697
It wasn't you, right? Chang-ho, please!

01:03:53.496 --> 01:03:55.748
SOLD OUT ON YOU

01:03:55.832 --> 01:04:01.754
THANKS TO SPECIAL GUEST SEO HYUN-WOO

01:05:00.813 --> 01:05:02.815
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park
